                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Count 5 outcomes with only the first die showing 3 and 5 with only the second showing 3.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "There are $36$ equally likely ordered outcomes. Exactly one die shows $3$ in two disjoint cases, each containing $5$ outcomes.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly one 3})&=\\frac{5+5}{36}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one 3})&=\\frac{10}{36}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one 3})&=\\frac{5}{18}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
